   "en": "§ The mishna teaches with regard to blood stains on garments that come «from among the Jews» and from among the Samaritans that Rabbi Meir deems them impure, and the Rabbis deem them ritually pure. The Gemara asks: «But» with regard to the opinion of «the Rabbis, if they deem» stains that come «from a Jewish» woman «pure, whose» stains «do they deem impure?»"
